{{Headline|25|In-game World Map}}

''<center>You can now access an in-game world map using the map icon beneath your minimap!</center>''


[[File:World Map & Balancing Changes (1).png|center]]


A simple left-click will open up a resizeable, moveable world map interface. You can also right-click the icon for a full screen option.

The resizeable, floating world map can be open as you play. You can even have other interfaces open alongside it.


[[File:World Map & Balancing Changes (2).png|center]]


Once open, the in-game world map has a number of useful functions.

If you wish to see a key, click the key button found in the bottom left of the interface.


[[File:World Map & Balancing Changes (3).png|center]]


Clicking on one of the items in the key will cause the icons on the map to briefly flash, allowing you to easily locate whatever it is you are looking for!


[[File:World Map & Balancing Changes (4).png|center]]


If you have the floating world map open, you can move it by clicking the border at the top and dragging.

If you wish to resize the window, click the border anywhere other than at the top of the world map window and drag to resize.


[[File:World Map & Balancing Changes (5).png|center]]


If you're struggling to find what you are looking for, you can try using the '''search function'''. Start typing for what you are looking for into the search box at the bottom of the world map window, and the search box will start auto-completing as you type.

Once you have typed what you are looking for, or auto-complete has suggested it, press enter and your world map will move to that location!


[[File:World Map & Balancing Changes (6).png|center]]


The search feature searches any map labels. So, if you are in a dungeon which lists the locations of monsters on the world map - you can search for the name of a monster and be taken to its location!

If you wish to view areas that are not on the surface of Gielinor, you can do so using '''map links'''!


[[File:World Map & Balancing Changes (7).png|center]]


Entrances across the surface of the world have map link icons which, when clicked, displays the destination of that entrance.

If you are in a complex dungeon, seeing which-entrance-goes-where can be very valuable. Luckily for you, the in-game world map also includes intra-map links!


[[File:World Map & Balancing Changes (8).png|center]]


If you are in a dungeon with a number of rooms or floors connected by different types of entrances, the world map will show you where those entrances will take you with intra-map links.


